 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "This is the topology half, the omission in Tag `03SI`. For a\nfamily $\\{U_i\\to U\\}$ of etale $X$-schemes, set\n$Z=|U|\\setminus\\bigcup_i\\operatorname{im}(|U_i|\\to|U|)$. Base change gives\na homeomorphism $|U\\times_XX_0|\\to|U|$, and its inverse image of $Z$ is\nexactly the complement of the union of the base-changed images. Hence\n$Z=\\varnothing$ if and only if that inverse image is empty. This proves\njoint surjectivity in both directions. The identity and composition\ncompatibilities already proved show that this correspondence of covering\nfamilies respects refinements and composite coverings.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
